1‡À`éí®Šò«Ó0XÛñcÓ®¥2ˆ„}×ª{"url":"/gcsl/language/failure/","fragment":{"page_number":0,"data":{"url":"/gcsl/language/failure/","content":"Failure. A program fails when it hits a runtime error: a panic, an index out of range, a program it runs exiting with an error, or a failed assert. Normally that ends the run. Two constructs work with failure directly: assert, which fails on purpose when something doesn't hold, and recover, which catches a failure and continues. Asserting # assert COND fails the run if the condition is false. The error shows the condition as you wrote it, and for a comparison it labels each side with its value, so a failed check explains itself: Copyerror: assertion failed: `output == \"hello\"` --> app.gcsl:2:8 | 2 | assert output == \"hello\" | ------ ------- this is `\"hello\"` | | | this is `\"hullo\"` Give your own message after a comma, assert ok, \"the server did not start\". Each side of a comparison is evaluated only once, so an assertion about a program's output doesn't run the program twice. Recovering # recover { BODY } else { FALLBACK } evaluates the body, and if it fails, evaluates the fallback instead. Name the failure to read its message: Copyfn half(n: Int): Int { assert n % 2 == 0, \"{n} is odd\" n // 2 } even = recover { half(10) } else { 0 } odd = recover { half(7) } else { -1 } message = recover { \"half is {half(7)}\" } else (failure) { failure.message } The failure is a record, {message: String}. The two blocks join as an if's branches do, so they normally have one type. recover catches what #[retry] would retry, and nothing else. A bug in GCSL itself is never caught. Neither is a timeout of a call that encloses the recover: that timeout belongs to the enclosing call, which ends as if the recover weren't there. A break, continue or return inside the body is not a failure, and leaves through it as usual. Anything the body did before it failed stays done.","word_count":328,"filters":{},"meta":{"crumbs":"GCSL / The Language","title":"Failure"},"anchors":[{"element":"h2","id":"asserting","text":"Asserting #","location":57},{"element":"h2","id":"recovering","text":"Recovering #","location":157}]}},"word_data":{"app":[{"position":102,"weight":12,"original_word":null}],"10":[{"position":207,"weight":12,"original_word":null}],"did":[{"position":133,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":322,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"so":[{"position":89,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":145,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":252,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"about":[{"position":148,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"never":[{"position":273,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"onli":[{"position":143,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"do":[{"position":251,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"doesn":[{"position":47,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":152,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"half":[{"position":186,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":207,"weight":12,"original_word":null},{"position":217,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":227,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":229,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"check":[{"position":92,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"enclos":[{"position":283,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":291,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"break":[{"position":302,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"error":[{"position":9,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":24,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":70,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"when":[{"position":4,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":45,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"2":[{"position":104,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":193,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":201,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"valu":[{"position":88,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"fallback":[{"position":165,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":176,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"record